    "summary": "Foxes hunting through fresh snow, photographed from a long way off and with a lot of patience.",
    "story": "<p>A fox in snow has nowhere to hide and knows it, so I stay well back, stay downwind and let the animal decide how close it wants to be. Most days it decides not to.</p><p>The best frame here came on the eleventh morning, about four minutes before I gave up.</p>",
